  message: "SATISFIED on merged dev 5e29e8d9b2, against this item's OWN filed repro re-run\non the merged tree rather than a proxy metric.\n\nTHE REPRO, four cells, map pinned by --input so the survey cache is not a\nvariable (it keys on repo CONTENT, and my first pass at this returned a stale\nauto-discovered map that answered the opposite way):\n\n                        BEFORE                  AFTER\n  armA boundary         confirmed  rc 0         confirmed  rc 0\n  armA taint            violated   rc 1         confirmed  rc 0   <- the defect\n  armB boundary         violated   rc 1         violated   rc 1\n  armB taint            violated   rc 1         violated   rc 1\n\narmA is one bash file whose only redirect is echo \"$API_KEY\" > /dev/null;\narmB is the identical script redirecting to /tmp/leak.txt. One cell moved and\nthe three control cells held.\n\nCHECK 1 OF THE ITEM'S OWN LIST, ANSWERED. The taint path decides a sink is real\nin _sink_call_can_carry_taint (taint.py), which is where BOTH propagators ask\nthe question -- taint.py's own comment at the structural call site says two\ncopies of it is how the call-family set drifted across three consumers. The\ndiscard clause lands there, beside the INV-fubag argument-shape proof, so it\ncannot be true of one arm and false of the other. Refusing upstream in\nclassify_call_in_catalog was deliberately NOT repeated: INV-nular measured that\nworse, because the coverage gate asks \"did the catalogue EXAMINE this call\" and\nthe answer is yes.\n\nCHECK 2, ANSWERED BY ENUMERATION RATHER THAN BY \"no known others\". Diffing what\neach path reads per call site: the io-boundary tagging loop consults\ncall_site_modes and call_site_target_kinds; the taint matcher consults\ncall_site_modes (both arms) and call_arg_shape (sink side only). Target kinds\nwere the ONLY fact one path used and the other did not, so this is a one-gate\ngap and not the tip of a family. The item was right to ask.\n\nCHECK 3, THE DIRECTION. Three controls ship with the fix -- an unresolved\ntarget (> \"$OUT\") still reports, a std_stream target still reports, and an edge\nwith no io_target_kind at all is untouched (default-deny on the silencing\ndirection). Plus the gate that catches the NEXT author: every behavioural test\npins null_device, so all of them would still pass if someone re-implemented the\ntaint clause against its own literal set, which is the one-fact-two-homes split\nthis item IS. One test therefore widens _DISCARDING_TARGET_KINDS at its single\nhome and asserts BOTH claim paths follow it to a value neither knew about, with\nthe unpatched assertion after it so the arms are proven to differ.\n\nMEASURED COST on the three repositories this item names, paired through the\nproduction CLI with the discarding vocabulary emptied to reproduce the pre-fix\npath (canary asserted: armed True / disarmed False):\n\n  cert-manager       37 -> 30 flows    evidence rows 9 -> 3\n  spacedrive         81 -> 74          evidence rows 9 -> 4\n  guacamole-client   12 -> 11          evidence rows 8 -> 7\n  TOTAL             130 -> 115         evidence rows 26 -> 14\n\nEvery removed row was read back against source and targets /dev/null. No real\nwrite was silenced.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ITEM'S ARITHMETIC, and it matters for whoever re-derives\n0006. The item says six of the eleven vacuity deductions are these six findings\nand implies all six leave. I cannot confirm that, and at least one will NOT:\ncert-manager's make/_shared/tools/util/lock.sh survives the fix CORRECTLY,\nbecause its `>` edge collapses line 35 (>/dev/null) with line 40\n(exec {FD}<>\"$lockfile\", target unresolved) and the gate requires EVERY\ncollapsed site to discard. If 0006 judged that row vacuous by reading line 35\nalone, the adjudication was wrong about the row rather than the row being\nwrongly kept. make/cluster.sh -- the instance this item reads against source --\ndoes clear.\n\nONE READING THAT LOOKED LIKE A LOST TRUE POSITIVE AND WAS NOT, recorded so the\nnext person does not file it: a checkhash.sh row appears \"new\" after the fix.\nIt is the same collapsed group with collapsed_flow_count 2 -> 1, its\nrepresentative primitive renamed from `>` to `>>` when the vacuous half left.\nThe real >> \"${LEARN_FILE:-}\" write is retained. Keying a pairing diff on the\nrepresentative primitive reports a shrink as a loss plus an addition.\n\nWHAT IS NOT WIRED, STATED RATHER THAN IMPLIED. The SOURCE side is not gated.\n< /dev/null yields EOF and is equally vacuous, but no boundary that can carry an\nio_target_kind stamp derives a taint source today: the stamp rides on bash\nredirects, and bash files `redirect` under fs_write/fs_read, neither of which is\nin AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP. An unreachable gate proves nothing, so instead a test\nre-derives that premise from every shipped catalogue and fails with the remedy\nif someone files redirect.< as ipc_recv. Its scope is disclosed in its own\ndocstring: it cannot see a SECOND analyzer starting to stamp the key, because\nthat code lives in the hypergumbo-lang-* packages, which CI tests in isolation\nfrom hypergumbo-core.\n\nTests: 3730 passed, 2 skipped, 2 xfailed; 100% coverage on changed sources;\nmypy strict ratchet clean at 669."  # f870
